<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<!--
  Bill-wise outstanding — V9 (2026-07-10)

  V4→V8 all embedded the TDL definition inline in the HTTP request. That
  doesn't work for <TYPE>Bill</TYPE> collections — Tally silently rejects
  or returns empty. V4 crashed loudly ("Could not find description"),
  V5→V8 returned empty responses on every sync.

  V9 = the proven 2-piece architecture from user's collaborator package
  (produced 2167 BILLROW rows on this exact Tally on 2026-07-09):

  Piece 1: TDKBillOutstanding.tdl — a full DSL TDL file that Tally
           loads to register the TDKBillOutstandingWorking report.
           Registered on demand via registerTdl() in util/xml.js
           (POST TDL to Tally over HTTP; happens once per sync).

  Piece 2 (this file): a minimal request envelope referencing the
           already-registered report by ID. NO inline TDL. Tally runs
           the pre-registered report and streams BILLROW rows.

  Response shape: <ENVELOPE><BILLROW>...</BILLROW>...</ENVELOPE>
  Encoding: UTF-16 LE with BOM (handled in getData via decodeTallyResponse).
  Fields per row: LedgerName, BillName, BillDate, DueDate, Amount,
                  PendingAmount, DrCr, LedgerParent

  Filtering (Dr-only, non-zero pending, per-ledger) happens in backend
  processBillOutstanding + /api/party/outstanding-bills — NOT in TDL.

  SVFROMDATE / SVTODATE scoped to current FY, substituted by desktop.
-->
<ENVELOPE>
  <HEADER>
    <VERSION>1</VERSION>
    <TALLYREQUEST>Export</TALLYREQUEST>
    <TYPE>Data</TYPE>
    <ID>TDKBillOutstandingWorking</ID>
  </HEADER>
  <BODY>
    <DESC>
      <STATICVARIABLES>
        <SVCURRENTCOMPANY>$$COMPANY_NAME</SVCURRENTCOMPANY>
        <SVEXPORTFORMAT>$$SysName:XML</SVEXPORTFORMAT>
        <SVFROMDATE TYPE="Date">$$FROM_DATE</SVFROMDATE>
        <SVTODATE TYPE="Date">$$TO_DATE</SVTODATE>
      </STATICVARIABLES>
    </DESC>
  </BODY>
</ENVELOPE>
